  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.7.0 — BEHAVIOUR CHANGE: Environment is now DETECTED instead of defaulting to the literal \"production\". It reads TOKENSBILL_ENVIRONMENT, ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT, DOTNET_ENVIRONMENT, APP_ENV or ENVIRONMENT (first match wins), folds short forms (prod/stg/uat/ci) to canonical names, passes unrecognised labels through unchanged, and reports \"unknown\" when nothing is set. Setting Environment explicitly still wins. Until now every staging and dev deployment reported its spend as production unless you configured this by hand, which silently broke exactly the prod-vs-non-prod comparisons the dashboard is for. After upgrading, expect non-production apps to start appearing under their real environment; historical events are unchanged. 0.4.8 — TokensBill.AspNetCore became the single SDK for tracking, utility functions (EstimateCost, EstimateTokens, CompareCosts, Deduplicate, RetryWithBudget) and AI functions (Summarize, ExtractJson, Classify, Chat, Embed). The separate TokensBill.AI package was deprecated in favour of it, and its source has now been removed.",
